materials_v2 READY, v2.1 (2026-11-24): weathered stone and organic trees. Full API in the header of scenes/materials_v2.js.

  const MV = require('./materials_v2')(S);        // S = your lik.js scene; one shared instance per scene

Stone (automatic, no opt-in): lik.js masonry/ashlar, battle_kit_b.flags, battle_li.rock, battle_kit_g1 flags/rubble/ring/rockMass,
battle_kit_g2 stoneCells/rockMass/smoothRock now weather themselves: per-stone tone, pits, spalls, chipped arrises, broken corners,
hairline and through cracks, worn edges, damp toward the base, lichen/moss, runs under ledges, mortar loss, and world variants
(salt, soot, frost, algae, weed). The world is guessed from the script name (bg_<world>_*.js, int_* = abbey_in, garth = abbey_out).
Per call: o.wx = false (off) | 'sea' | { world: 'rime', decay: 1.3, lichen: 0 }. Env MV2_OFF=1 turns it all off.
Marks use their own random stream: room geometry and every S.R placement stay identical. Detail thins with depth and is capped
per plane and per scene, so layers stay under ~5 MB.

New stone helpers:
  MV.hewnRock(at, Ls, Lt, col, { bed, dip, joint, tool, wx })   natural/rock-cut face: strata, fractures, no mortar
  MV.rockSkin(pts, Z, col, { wx, strata })                      the same weathering inside a screen outline
  MV.weatherWall / MV.weatherFloor (at, Ls, Lt, wx)             plane-level runs, damp band, cracks / worn path, puddles, frost
  MV.stoneMarks(ps, Z, fill, { wy0, wx })                       marks for one loose stone polygon

Trees and strands (screen space, (x, y) = ground point):
  MV.tree(x, y, h, Z, { kind: oak|dead|yew|alder|birch|fungal|frozen|pollard|windswept|snag, col, lean, leaves, seed })
      -> { svg, limbs, trunk, tw, wAt, tips }  (root flare into a ground lip; never floats)
  MV.renderTree({ trunk, trunkW: [w0, w1], limbs: [[pts, w0, w1]] }, Z, { kind, col })   draw your own skeleton organically
  MV.strand(pts, w0, w1, Z), MV.vine(A, B, Z), MV.hangRoots(x0, x1, y, Z), MV.surfaceRoots(x, y, w, Z), MV.kelp(x, y, h, Z)
battle_kit_g5.tree and battle_kit_g4.roots already draw through it (same skeleton, same return value, same random stream).

Test sheet: out/scenes/materials_v2_sheet.png. Before/after rooms: out/scenes/materials_v2/{before,after}/.

v2.1 (reads at 1x): per-stone tone and hue (darker / warmer / cooler / bleached; a lighter palette on dark stone), weathering
zones that run across courses, the odd fallen-out stone, larger chipped arrises and broken corners with a dark recess and lit
lip, dark lost-mortar joints with grime and moss in them, a damp/grime gradient over the bottom third of every wall, soot
climbing above the room's lights (filled in at write time), runs under ledges, floor slabs with worn dips, cracks, missing
corners and dirt in the joints; fewer pin pits, more mid-size pocks. Yew: dense dark merged masses, trunk mostly hidden.
Big single shapes (rockSkin outlines, frame-tall stoneMarks shapes) get local marks only: no whole-shape washes, no pale ovals,
lit lips relative to the base tone (dark earth stays dark); runs tinted from the plane's own stone colour. The g2 size guard on
smoothRock is removed. Weight: marks are capped per plane (by depth and by the plane's own stone bytes) and per scene, and thin
out on layers already over ~3.4 MB; wall stones now write texture, hatch and heavy ink once per plane, so most layers end close
to their old size. MV2_DEBUG=1 prints per-plane mark bytes.
